    "field": "argument_node.doc",
    "value": "Splitting off one realised value at a point of S where the family is not constant strictly lowers the number of traces, because a second value survives outside the branch."
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.pretty",
    "value": "∀ {X : Type u_1} {Y : Type u_2} {𝒞 : Set (X → Y)} {S : Set X} {x : X} {u : Y},\n  x ∈ S →\n    ∀ {c : X → Y},\n      c ∈ 𝒞 → c x ≠ u → (S.restrict '' 𝒞).Finite → (S.restrict '' {d | d ∈ 𝒞 ∧ d x = u}).ncard < (S.restrict '' 𝒞).ncard"
  },
